"ctet-q-0001","ctet-p2","ctet-math","ctet-math-c1","ctet-math-t1","2024","January 2024","If x = 2³ × 3² × 5³ × 7³, y = 2² × 3³ × 5⁴ × 7³ and z = 2⁴ × 3⁴ × 5² × 7⁵, then the Highest Common Factor (HCF) of x, y and z is:","2² × 3² × 5² × 7³","2³ × 3³ × 5³ × 7⁴","2⁴ × 3⁴ × 5⁴ × 7⁵","2² × 3² × 5³ × 7³","","A","To find HCF from prime powers, take the minimum power of each common prime factor: 2^min(3,2,4)=2², 3^min(2,3,4)=3², 5^min(3,4,2)=5², 7^min(3,3,5)=7³. Thus HCF = 2² × 3² × 5² × 7³.","CTET Jan 2024 Paper 2 (Mathematics, Set K, Q. 31)","official_pyq_verified","Verified Official PYQ","Moderate","2026-10-13T06:05:20Z"
"ctet-q-0002","ctet-p2","ctet-math","ctet-math-c2","ctet-math-t3","2023","August 2023","Which of the following is an open-ended question in a middle-school Mathematics classroom?","Find the perimeter of a rectangle having length 12 cm and breadth 8 cm.","Write any two pairs of whole numbers whose sum is 45.","Solve for x: 3x + 7 = 22.","What is the square root of 289?","","B","An open-ended question admits multiple solutions and problem-solving approaches. Finding pairs of whole numbers adding up to 45 has multiple correct responses, fostering divergent mathematical reasoning.","CTET Aug 2023 Paper 2 (Math Pedagogy, Q. 42)","official_pyq_verified","Verified Official PYQ","Easy","2026-10-13T06:05:20Z"
"ctet-q-0003","ctet-p2","ctet-math","ctet-math-c2","ctet-math-t4","2023","August 2023","According to Van Hiele’s geometric thinking model, when a student perceives relationships between properties of figures (e.g., 'every square is a rectangle') and understands informal arguments, the student is operating at:","Level 0 (Visualization)","Level 1 (Analysis)","Level 2 (Abstraction / Informal Deduction)","Level 3 (Formal Deduction)","","C","At Level 2 (Abstraction/Informal Deduction), learners understand hierarchical classifications (e.g. squares are rectangles) and evaluate informal geometric proofs.","CTET Aug 2023 Paper 2 (Math Pedagogy, Q. 48)","official_pyq_verified","Verified Official PYQ","Moderate","2026-10-13T06:05:20Z"
"ctet-q-0004","ctet-p2","ctet-math","ctet-math-c1","ctet-math-t2","2022","December 2022","A sum of ₹12,000 is lent at 10% per annum for 1½ years. If interest is compounded half-yearly, what is the compound interest accrued?","₹1,891.50","₹1,800.00","₹1,950.00","₹2,025.50","","A","Half-yearly rate r = 10/2 = 5%. Conversion periods n = 1.5 × 2 = 3. Amount A = 12000 × (1.05)³ = ₹13,891.50. CI = ₹1,891.50.","CTET Dec 2022 Paper 2 (Mathematics, Q. 36)","official_pyq_verified","Verified Official PYQ","Challenging","2026-10-13T06:05:20Z"
"ctet-q-0005","ctet-p2","ctet-sci","ctet-sci-c1","ctet-sci-t1","2024","January 2024","Which of the following statements correctly distinguishes evaporation from boiling?","Evaporation is a bulk phenomenon, whereas boiling is a surface phenomenon.","Evaporation takes place at any temperature below the boiling point, whereas boiling occurs only at a definite fixed temperature.","Boiling causes cooling of the surrounding liquid, whereas evaporation causes heating.","Evaporation involves bubble formation throughout the liquid mass, whereas boiling does not.","","B","Evaporation is a surface phenomenon occurring at any temperature below boiling point causing cooling. Boiling is a bulk phenomenon occurring strictly at boiling point.","CTET Jan 2024 Paper 2 (Science, Set K, Q. 62)","official_pyq_verified","Verified Official PYQ","Easy","2026-10-13T06:05:20Z"
"ctet-q-0006","ctet-p2","ctet-sci","ctet-sci-c1","ctet-sci-t2","2023","August 2023","A student adds drops of phenolphthalein indicator to test tube A (dilute sodium hydroxide) and test tube B (dilute hydrochloric acid). What observation will the student record?","Test tube A turns pink; test tube B remains colorless.","Test tube A turns blue; test tube B turns red.","Test tube A remains colorless; test tube B turns pink.","Both test tubes turn bright yellow.","","A","Phenolphthalein indicator turns pink in alkaline solutions (NaOH) and remains colorless in acidic solutions (HCl).","CTET Aug 2023 Paper 2 (Science, Set E, Q. 67)","official_pyq_verified","Verified Official PYQ","Easy","2026-10-13T06:05:20Z"
"ctet-q-0007","ctet-p2","ctet-sci","ctet-sci-c3","ctet-sci-t5","2023","August 2023","An object is placed in front of a concave mirror between its pole (P) and principal focus (F). The nature of the image formed is:","Real, inverted and magnified","Real, inverted and diminished","Virtual, erect and magnified","Virtual, erect and diminished","","C","When placed between pole and focus of a concave mirror, rays diverge after reflection and appear to meet behind the mirror, creating a virtual, erect, and magnified image.","CTET Aug 2023 Paper 2 (Science, Q. 75)","official_pyq_verified","Verified Official PYQ","Moderate","2026-10-13T06:05:20Z"
"ctet-q-0008","ctet-p2","ctet-sci","ctet-sci-c4","ctet-sci-t7","2024","January 2024","Which of the following human organs functions as both an exocrine gland (secreting digestive enzymes) and an endocrine gland (secreting hormones into blood)?","Thyroid gland","Liver","Pancreas","Adrenal gland","","C","The pancreas has exocrine acini that secrete digestive enzymes and endocrine Islets of Langerhans that secrete insulin and glucagon into the blood.","CTET Jan 2024 Paper 2 (Science, Set K, Q. 81)","official_pyq_verified","Verified Official PYQ","Easy","2026-10-13T06:05:20Z"
