"ctet-q-0125","ctet-p2","ctet-math","ctet-math-c1","ctet-math-t1","","","If x = 2^2 × 3^2 × 5², y = 2^1 × 3^3 × 5³ and z = 2^3 × 3^1 × 5, what is the Highest Common Factor (HCF) of x, y and z?","2^1 × 3^1 × 5","2^2 × 3^2 × 5²","2^3 × 3^3 × 5³","2^1 × 3^2 × 5","","A","To compute the HCF of numbers in prime factorized form, select the minimum power of each common prime base:
• Power of 2: min(2, 1, 3) = 1
• Power of 3: min(2, 3, 1) = 1
• Power of 5: min(2, 3, 1) = 1
Therefore, HCF = 2^1 × 3^1 × 5.","","original_practice","Verified Syllabus Practice","Moderate","2026-10-13T06:05:20Z"
