"ctet-q-0193","ctet-p2","ctet-math","ctet-math-c1","ctet-math-t4","","","A principal of ₹8000 is invested at 5% per annum for 2 years. What is the difference between the Compound Interest (compounded annually) and the Simple Interest earned on this amount?","₹20.00","₹70.00","₹45.00","₹30.00","","A","Step 1: Calculate Simple Interest (SI):
SI = (P × R × T) / 100 = (8000 × 5 × 2) / 100 = ₹800.00

Step 2: Calculate Compound Interest (CI):
Amount = P × (1 + R/100)^T = 8000 × (1 + 5/100)^2 = ₹8820.00
CI = Amount - Principal = ₹820.00

Step 3: Difference:
CI - SI = ₹820.00 - ₹800.00 = ₹20.00.","","original_practice","Verified Syllabus Practice","Moderate","2026-10-13T06:05:20Z"
"ctet-q-0194","ctet-p2","ctet-math","ctet-math-c1","ctet-math-t4","","","A principal of ₹10000 is invested at 10% per annum for 2 years. What is the difference between the Compound Interest (compounded annually) and the Simple Interest earned on this amount?","₹100.00","₹150.00","₹75.00","₹150.00","","A","Step 1: Calculate Simple Interest (SI):
SI = (P × R × T) / 100 = (10000 × 10 × 2) / 100 = ₹2000.00

Step 2: Calculate Compound Interest (CI):
Amount = P × (1 + R/100)^T = 10000 × (1 + 10/100)^2 = ₹12100.00
CI = Amount - Principal = ₹2100.00

Step 3: Difference:
CI - SI = ₹2100.00 - ₹2000.00 = ₹100.00.","","original_practice","Verified Syllabus Practice","Moderate","2026-10-13T06:05:20Z"
"ctet-q-0195","ctet-p2","ctet-math","ctet-math-c1","ctet-math-t4","","","A principal of ₹12000 is invested at 8% per annum for 2 years. What is the difference between the Compound Interest (compounded annually) and the Simple Interest earned on this amount?","₹76.80","₹126.80","₹51.80","₹115.20","","A","Step 1: Calculate Simple Interest (SI):
