"ctet-q-0201","ctet-p2","ctet-math","ctet-math-c2","ctet-math-t8","","","Solve the linear equation for x: 2x + 2 = 4(x - 3). What is the value of x?","x = 7","x = 9","x = 4","x = 14","","A","Expanding the right hand side:
2x + 2 = 4x - 12
Rearranging terms with x to one side:
2 + 12 = 4x - 2x
14 = 2x
x = 14 / 2 = 7.","","original_practice","Verified Syllabus Practice","Easy","2026-10-13T06:05:20Z"
"ctet-q-0202","ctet-p2","ctet-math","ctet-math-c2","ctet-math-t8","","","Solve the linear equation for x: 4x + 2 = 6(x - 3). What is the value of x?","x = 10","x = 12","x = 7","x = 20","","A","Expanding the right hand side:
4x + 2 = 6x - 18
Rearranging terms with x to one side:
2 + 18 = 6x - 4x
20 = 2x
x = 20 / 2 = 10.","","original_practice","Verified Syllabus Practice","Easy","2026-10-13T06:05:20Z"
"ctet-q-0203","ctet-p2","ctet-math","ctet-math-c3","ctet-math-t11","","","In triangle ABC, the interior opposite angles to an exterior angle at vertex C measure 50° and 60°. What is the measure of the exterior angle at vertex C?","110°","70°","125°","90°","","A","According to the Exterior Angle Theorem of a triangle, an exterior angle equals the sum of its two interior opposite angles:
