"ctet-q-0219","ctet-p2","ctet-math","ctet-math-c4","ctet-math-t18","","","A student identifies that 'all rectangles are parallelograms and all squares are rectangles' based on formal logical definitions of inclusion. According to the Van Hiele model, at which level is the student functioning?","Level 2 (Abstraction / Informal Deduction)","Level 0 (Visualization / Recognition)","Level 1 (Analysis / Descriptive)","Level 3 (Rigor)","","A","At Van Hiele Level 2 (Abstraction / Informal Deduction), learners perceive relationships between properties of figures and comprehend class inclusions (e.g., squares are a subset of rectangles).","","original_practice","Verified Syllabus Practice","Moderate","2026-10-13T06:05:20Z"
"ctet-q-0220","ctet-p2","ctet-math","ctet-math-c4","ctet-math-t18","","","When a 6th grade child judges a shape as a square only because 'it looks like a window or a tile', without analyzing its side lengths or perpendicular angles, the child is at:","Level 0 (Visualization)","Level 1 (Analysis)","Level 2 (Informal Deduction)","Level 3 (Formal Deduction)","","A","At Level 0 (Visualization), shapes are judged holistically by physical appearance rather than by mathematical properties.","","original_practice","Verified Syllabus Practice","Moderate","2026-10-13T06:05:20Z"
"ctet-q-0221","ctet-p2","ctet-math","ctet-math-c4","ctet-math-t16","","","Which of the following characteristics best describes the nature of mathematical knowledge?","It is hierarchical, deductive, and conceptual","It is purely empirical and based only on sensory observation","It is arbitrary and subjective to cultural opinions","It relies entirely on rote memorization of algorithms","","A","Mathematics is inherently structured hierarchically (concepts build upon prior foundations) and relies on rigorous deductive reasoning and conceptual abstraction.","","original_practice","Verified Syllabus Practice","Moderate","2026-10-13T06:05:20Z"
"ctet-q-0222","ctet-p2","ctet-math","ctet-math-c4","ctet-math-t19","","","A middle school student computes 1/3 + 1/4 = 2/7. As a mathematics teacher, how should you diagnose and remedy this systematic error?","Use concrete fraction strips to visually demonstrate common denominators and equivalent parts","Give the child 50 identical drills to write the algorithm repeatedly","Deduct marks and inform parents about careless arithmetic","Ask the child to copy the solution from the blackboard","","A","Adding numerators and denominators directly (1/3 + 1/4 = 2/7) is a common misconception where whole number addition is overgeneralized to fractions. Concrete manipulatives (fraction strips or area models) help establish conceptual understanding of common partitions.","","original_practice","Verified Syllabus Practice","Moderate","2026-10-13T06:05:20Z"
"ctet-q-0223","ctet-p2","ctet-math","ctet-math-c4","ctet-math-t20","","","Which of the following is an effective open-ended question in a middle school mathematics classroom?","Find any three pairs of prime numbers whose difference is 6.","What is the square of 17?","Find the area of a square whose side is 8 cm.","Solve: 4x + 5 = 25.","","A","Open-ended questions have multiple entry points and diverse correct answers (e.g., (5,11), (7,13), (11,17)), promoting divergent mathematical reasoning, exploration, and problem formulation.","","original_practice","Verified Syllabus Practice","Moderate","2026-10-13T06:05:20Z"
"ctet-q-0224","ctet-p2","ctet-math","ctet-math-c4","ctet-math-t21","","","The primary objective of diagnostic testing in elementary mathematics is to:","Identify specific conceptual gaps and root causes of learning difficulties","Rank students in order of academic merit for report cards","Assign grades and pass/fail verdicts at the end of the term","Complete syllabus formalities within the allotted time","","A","Diagnostic assessment aims specifically to pinpoint learning deficits, misconceptions, and procedural gaps so that targeted remedial interventions can be designed.","","original_practice","Verified Syllabus Practice","Moderate","2026-10-13T06:05:20Z"
"ctet-q-0225","ctet-p2","ctet-sci","ctet-sci-c1","ctet-sci-t1","","","Why does water kept in an earthen pot (matka) become cool during hot summer days?","Continuous evaporation through porous walls absorbs latent heat of vaporization from the water","Earthen pots create endothermic chemical reactions with dissolved minerals","Clay reflects all incoming infrared thermal radiation completely","Air inside the pot contracts and undergoes adiabatic compression","","A","An earthen pot has microscopic pores through which water continuously seeps out. As this water evaporates into the dry surrounding air, it absorbs the latent heat of vaporization from the remaining water and pot surface, resulting in cooling.","","original_practice","Verified Syllabus Practice","Moderate","2026-10-13T06:05:20Z"
"ctet-q-0226","ctet-p2","ctet-sci","ctet-sci-c3","ctet-sci-t2","","","When a drop of phenolphthalein indicator is added to a test tube containing sodium hydroxide (NaOH) solution, the color turns:","Deep pink","Bright yellow","Colorless","Brick red","","A","Phenolphthalein is a synthetic indicator that remains colorless in acidic and neutral solutions but turns distinct pink in basic/alkaline solutions (such as NaOH).","","original_practice","Verified Syllabus Practice","Moderate","2026-10-13T06:05:20Z"
"ctet-q-0227","ctet-p2","ctet-sci","ctet-sci-c3","ctet-sci-t4","","","An iron nail is dipped into a blue copper sulphate (CuSO₄) solution. After 30 minutes, what observable change takes place?","The blue solution turns pale light green and a reddish-brown coating forms on the nail","The blue solution turns milky white and gas bubbles evolve violently","The solution becomes completely colorless and the nail dissolves completely","No reaction occurs because copper is more reactive than iron","","A","Iron is placed above copper in the reactivity series. Iron displaces copper from CuSO₄ solution forming iron(II) sulphate (FeSO₄), which turns the solution light green, while reddish-brown metallic copper deposits on the iron nail: Fe + CuSO₄ → FeSO₄ + Cu.","","original_practice","Verified Syllabus Practice","Moderate","2026-10-13T06:05:20Z"
"ctet-q-0228","ctet-p2","ctet-sci","ctet-sci-c2","ctet-sci-t6","","","Which of the following plants is an insectivorous plant that performs photosynthesis but traps insects to supplement nitrogen deficiency?","Pitcher plant (Nepenthes)","Cuscuta (Amarbel)","Mushroom (Agaricus)","Bread mould (Rhizopus)","","A","Pitcher plants contain chlorophyll and carry out photosynthesis to produce carbohydrates. However, because they grow in nitrogen-deficient bogs, they trap and digest insects to fulfill their nitrogen requirements.","","original_practice","Verified Syllabus Practice","Moderate","2026-10-13T06:05:20Z"
"ctet-q-0229","ctet-p2","ctet-sci","ctet-sci-c2","ctet-sci-t8","","","During vigorous muscular exercise in humans, sudden muscle cramps occur due to the accumulation of:","Lactic acid caused by anaerobic breakdown of glucose","Carbon dioxide caused by hyperventilation","Alcohol and acetic acid inside muscle cells","Uric acid crystals in the knee joints","","A","When oxygen supply to muscle tissues is insufficient during intense physical activity, muscle cells undergo anaerobic respiration, breaking down pyruvate into lactic acid. The accumulation of lactic acid leads to painful muscle cramps.","","original_practice","Verified Syllabus Practice","Moderate","2026-10-13T06:05:20Z"
"ctet-q-0230","ctet-p2","ctet-sci","ctet-sci-c2","ctet-sci-t9","","","In the human excretory system, what is the functional microscopic unit responsible for filtration of blood and formation of urine?","Nephron","Neuron","Alveolus","Villus","","A","The nephron is the structural and functional unit of the human kidney. Each kidney contains approximately one million nephrons which carry out ultrafiltration, selective reabsorption, and secretion.","","original_practice","Verified Syllabus Practice","Moderate","2026-10-13T06:05:20Z"
"ctet-q-0231","ctet-p2","ctet-sci","ctet-sci-c3","ctet-sci-t16","","","Which type of mirror is universally used as a rear-view mirror in automobiles to provide a wide field of view?","Convex mirror","Concave mirror","Plane mirror","Cylindrical mirror","","A","Convex mirrors always form erect, virtual, and diminished images of distant objects. Because they curve outward, they afford drivers a considerably wider field of view than flat plane mirrors.","","original_practice","Verified Syllabus Practice","Moderate","2026-10-13T06:05:20Z"
"ctet-q-0232","ctet-p2","ctet-sci","ctet-sci-c3","ctet-sci-t17","","","An electric fuse wire used in household circuits must possess which of the following physical characteristics?","High resistance and low melting point","Low resistance and high melting point","High resistance and high melting point","Low resistance and low melting point","","A","A fuse wire must generate sufficient Joule heat (H = I²Rt) when excessive current flows, hence requires high resistance, and must melt rapidly to break the circuit, requiring a low melting point.","","original_practice","Verified Syllabus Practice","Moderate","2026-10-13T06:05:20Z"
"ctet-q-0233","ctet-p2","ctet-sci","ctet-sci-c4","ctet-sci-t19","","","According to the National Curriculum Framework (NCF-2005), which criterion ensures that upper primary science curriculum engages learners in exploring processes through hands-on activities?","Process validity","Cognitive validity","Historical validity","Ethical validity","","A","Process validity requires that the curriculum engages students in learning the methods, processes, and systematic inquiry of science through observation, classification, and experimentation.","","original_practice","Verified Syllabus Practice","Moderate","2026-10-13T06:05:20Z"
"ctet-q-0234","ctet-p2","ctet-sci","ctet-sci-c4","ctet-sci-t21","","","While introducing the topic of 'Rusting of Iron', the most pedagogically appropriate starting activity for a science teacher is to:","Ask students to set up test tubes with iron nails under dry air, boiled water, and moist air conditions and observe over several days","Write the balanced chemical redox equation directly on the board and ask students to memorize it","Distribute a printed worksheet with definitions of oxidation numbers","Dictate answers to the end-of-chapter textbook exercise","","A","Inquiry-based experiential learning starts with authentic observation and controlled experimentation. Observing nails in varying conditions allows middle-school learners to deduce the necessary factors (water + oxygen) actively.","","original_practice","Verified Syllabus Practice","Moderate","2026-10-13T06:05:20Z"
"ctet-q-0235","ctet-p2","ctet-sci","ctet-sci-c4","ctet-sci-t22","","","Which assessment tool is most appropriate for assessing students' collaborative inquiry skills, laboratory hygiene, and experimental manipulation during practical science tasks?","Analytic Rubric with clear observable criteria","Multiple-choice written term examination","True/False recall speed test","Oral recitation test","","A","Rubrics provide structured, objective criteria and performance descriptors for assessing complex psychomotor and social behaviors in inquiry tasks.","","original_practice","Verified Syllabus Practice","Moderate","2026-10-13T06:05:20Z"
