"ctet-q-0314","ctet-p2","ctet-math","ctet-math-c1","ctet-math-t4","","","A shopkeeper marks an article at ₹5500 and offers a discount of 6%. If the cost price is ₹4840, what is the percentage profit or loss on this transaction? (Variant 1)","Profit of 6.8%","Loss of 6%","No profit no loss","Profit of 10%","","A","Selling Price = 5500 × (1 - 6/100) = ₹5170.00.
Cost Price = ₹4840.
Profit = Selling Price - Cost Price. Profit % is calculated with respect to Cost Price.","","original_practice","Verified Syllabus Practice","Moderate","2026-10-13T06:05:20Z"
