"stet-q-0376","bihar-stet-p1","stet-math","stet-math-c1","stet-math-t4","","","For the quadratic equation x² + 6x + 2 = 0, what is the value of the discriminant (D) and the nature of its roots? (Variant 1)","D = 28, having two distinct real roots","D = 44, having imaginary roots","D = -28, having irrational roots","D = 0, having one real root","","A","For ax² + bx + c = 0, the discriminant is given by D = b² - 4ac.
Here a = 1, b = 6, c = 2.
D = (6)² - 4(1)(2) = 36 - 8 = 28.
Since D > 0, the equation has two distinct real roots.","","original_practice","Verified Syllabus Practice","Moderate","2026-10-13T06:05:20Z"
