"stet-q-0568","bihar-stet-p1","stet-math","stet-math-c3","stet-math-t10","","","A vertical tower casts a shadow of length 10 m on level ground when the sun's angle of elevation is 45°. What is the height of the tower? (Variant 1)","10 m","20 m","5.0 m","25 m","","A","In a right triangle formed by the vertical tower (h) and horizontal shadow (d = 10 m):
tan(45°) = Height / Shadow = h / 10.
