"stet-q-0728","bihar-stet-p1","stet-sci","stet-sci-c1","stet-sci-t1","","","A particle starts with an initial velocity u = 5 m/s and moves in a straight line with uniform acceleration a = 2 m/s². What distance does it cover in t = 4 seconds? (Variant 1)","36 m","13 m","46 m","20 m","","A","Using the second equation of motion for uniform acceleration:
s = ut + (1/2)at²
s = (5)(4) + 0.5(2)(4²) = 20 + 16.0 = 36 m.","","original_practice","Verified Syllabus Practice","Moderate","2026-10-13T06:05:20Z"
