"bpsc-mid-q-0001","bpsc-tre-middle","bpsc-mid-sci","bpsc-mid-sci-c1","bpsc-mid-sci-t1","2023","TRE 2.0 (Dec 2023)","An electric heater having a heating coil of resistance 50 Ω draws a current of 4 A from a circuit for 2 minutes. The heat energy produced in the coil is:","96,000 J","4,800 J","24,000 J","More than one of the above","None of the above","A","H = I²Rt = (4)² × 50 × (2 × 60) = 16 × 50 × 120 = 96,000 J.","BPSC TRE 2.0 Middle Stage (Classes 6-8 Math & Science, Q. 73)","official_pyq_verified","Verified Official PYQ","Moderate","2026-10-13T06:05:20Z"
"bpsc-mid-q-0002","bpsc-tre-middle","bpsc-mid-sci","bpsc-mid-sci-c2","bpsc-mid-sci-t2","2023","TRE 1.0 (Aug 2023)","According to Lindeman's 10% ecological law, if producers in an ecosystem trap 10,000 J of solar energy into organic matter, how much energy is transferred to secondary consumers?","100 J","1,000 J","10 J","More than one of the above","None of the above","A","Producers: 10,000 J -> Herbivores: 1,000 J -> Secondary Consumers (Carnivores): 100 J.","BPSC TRE 1.0 Middle Stage Science, Q. 84","official_pyq_verified","Verified Official PYQ","Easy","2026-10-13T06:05:20Z"
"bpsc-mid-q-0003","bpsc-tre-middle","bpsc-mid-sci","bpsc-mid-sci-c2","bpsc-mid-sci-t3","2023","TRE 2.0 (Dec 2023)","In the mammalian kidney, the basic structural and functional filtration unit responsible for ultrafiltration and selective reabsorption is called the:","Neuron","Nephron","Alveolus","More than one of the above","None of the above","B","The nephron is the microscopic filtration unit of the kidney. Neurons are nerve cells, alveoli are lung units, villi are small intestine units.","BPSC TRE 2.0 Middle Stage (Classes 6-8 Math & Science, Q. 92)","official_pyq_verified","Verified Official PYQ","Easy","2026-10-13T06:05:20Z"
"bpsc-mid-q-0004","bpsc-tre-middle","bpsc-mid-math","bpsc-mid-math-c1","bpsc-mid-math-t1","2024","TRE 3.0 (March 2024)","A can complete a piece of work in 12 days, and B can complete the same work in 18 days. If they work together on the task, in how many days will the entire work be completed?","7.2 days","6.0 days","8.5 days","More than one of the above","None of the above","A","Rate A = 1/12, Rate B = 1/18. Combined = 5/36 per day. Total time = 36/5 = 7.2 days.","BPSC TRE 3.0 Middle Stage (Classes 6-8 Math, Q. 35)","official_pyq_verified","Verified Official PYQ","Easy","2026-10-13T06:05:20Z"
"bpsc-mid-q-0005","bpsc-tre-middle","bpsc-mid-math","bpsc-mid-math-c1","bpsc-mid-math-t2","2023","TRE 2.0 (Dec 2023)","If the price of sugar increases by 25%, by what percentage must a household reduce its consumption so that its expenditure on sugar remains unchanged?","20%","25%","16.67%","More than one of the above","None of the above","A","Consumption reduction = [R / (100 + R)] × 100% = [25 / 125] × 100% = 20%.","BPSC TRE 2.0 Middle Stage (Classes 6-8 Math, Q. 48)","official_pyq_verified","Verified Official PYQ","Easy","2026-10-13T06:05:20Z"
"bpsc-mid-q-0006","bpsc-tre-middle","bpsc-mid-sci","bpsc-mid-sci-c2","bpsc-mid-sci-t3","2023","TRE 2.0 (Dec 2023)","Bile juice is secreted by which organ of the human digestive system, and where is it temporarily stored before being released into the duodenum?","Secreted by Pancreas, stored in Stomach","Secreted by Liver, stored in Gallbladder","Secreted by Salivary glands, stored in Liver","More than one of the above","None of the above","B","Bile juice is synthesized by hepatocytes in the liver and stored/concentrated in the gallbladder until released during digestion.","BPSC TRE 2.0 Middle Stage (Classes 6-8 Math & Science, Q. 88)","official_pyq_verified","Verified Official PYQ","Easy","2026-10-13T06:05:20Z"
