"bpsc-mid-q-0190","bpsc-tre-middle","bpsc-mid-math","bpsc-mid-math-c1","bpsc-mid-math-t3","","","A merchant marks goods 25% above the Cost Price (CP = ₹420) and offers a discount of 10% on the Marked Price. What is the net profit percentage earned by the merchant? (Variant 1)","12.50%","15.00%","17.50%","More than one of the above","None of the above","A","Let CP = ₹420.
Marked Price (MP) = 420 × (1 + 25/100) = ₹525.00.
Selling Price (SP) = 525.00 × (1 - 10/100) = ₹472.50.
Profit = SP - CP = ₹52.50.
Profit % = [(52.50) / 420] × 100 = 12.50%.","","original_practice","Verified Syllabus Practice","Moderate","2026-10-13T06:05:20Z"
"bpsc-mid-q-0191","bpsc-tre-middle","bpsc-mid-math","bpsc-mid-math-c1","bpsc-mid-math-t3","","","A merchant marks goods 30% above the Cost Price (CP = ₹440) and offers a discount of 10% on the Marked Price. What is the net profit percentage earned by the merchant? (Variant 2)","17.00%","20.00%","22.00%","More than one of the above","None of the above","A","Let CP = ₹440.
Marked Price (MP) = 440 × (1 + 30/100) = ₹572.00.
Selling Price (SP) = 572.00 × (1 - 10/100) = ₹514.80.
Profit = SP - CP = ₹74.80.
Profit % = [(74.80) / 440] × 100 = 17.00%.","","original_practice","Verified Syllabus Practice","Moderate","2026-10-13T06:05:20Z"
