"bpsc-mid-q-0745","bpsc-tre-middle","bpsc-mid-sci","bpsc-mid-sci-c1","bpsc-mid-sci-t5","","","An electric appliance having resistance R = 6 Ω is operated across a potential difference of V = 14 V. What is the electric power consumed by the appliance? (Variant 1)","32.7 W","2.3 W","84.0 W","More than one of the above","None of the above","A","According to Joule's law of electric power:
P = V² / R = (14²) / 6 = 196 / 6 = 32.7 W.
Equivalently, Current I = V / R = 2.3 A, and P = V × I = 14 × 2.3 = 32.7 W.","","original_practice","Verified Syllabus Practice","Easy","2026-10-13T06:05:20Z"
"bpsc-mid-q-0746","bpsc-tre-middle","bpsc-mid-sci","bpsc-mid-sci-c1","bpsc-mid-sci-t5","","","An electric appliance having resistance R = 8 Ω is operated across a potential difference of V = 16 V. What is the electric power consumed by the appliance? (Variant 2)","32.0 W","2.0 W","128.0 W","More than one of the above","None of the above","A","According to Joule's law of electric power:
P = V² / R = (16²) / 8 = 256 / 8 = 32.0 W.
