"bpsc-sec-q-0001","bpsc-tre-secondary","bpsc-sec-phy","bpsc-sec-phy-c1","bpsc-sec-phy-t1","2023","TRE 2.0 (Dec 2023)","A person cannot clearly see objects closer than 75 cm. What is the power of the corrective lens required to restore normal near vision (least distance of distinct vision D = 25 cm)?","+2.67 D","-2.67 D","+1.33 D","More than one of the above","None of the above","A","u = -25 cm = -0.25 m, v = -75 cm = -0.75 m. 1/f = 1/v - 1/u = 1/(-0.75) - 1/(-0.25) = -1.33 + 4.00 = +2.67 m⁻¹ => Power P = +2.67 D.","BPSC TRE 2.0 Secondary Science (Class 9-10, Q. 82)","official_pyq_verified","Verified Official PYQ","Moderate","2026-10-13T06:05:20Z"
"bpsc-sec-q-0002","bpsc-tre-secondary","bpsc-sec-chem","bpsc-sec-chem-c1","bpsc-sec-chem-t1","2023","TRE 2.0 (Dec 2023)","What is the total number of structural isomers possible for the saturated alkane pentane (C₅H₁₂)?","2","3","4","More than one of the above","None of the above","B","Pentane (C₅H₁₂) has 3 structural chain isomers: n-pentane, isopentane (2-methylbutane), and neopentane (2,2-dimethylpropane).","BPSC TRE 2.0 Secondary Science (Class 9-10, Q. 104)","official_pyq_verified","Verified Official PYQ","Moderate","2026-10-13T06:05:20Z"
"bpsc-sec-q-0003","bpsc-tre-secondary","bpsc-sec-bio","bpsc-sec-bio-c1","bpsc-sec-bio-t1","2023","TRE 1.0 (Aug 2023)","In a classical Mendelian dihybrid cross involving pea plants heterozygous for seed shape and seed color (RrYy × RrYy), what is the phenotypic ratio obtained in the F2 generation?","9:3:3:1","1:2:1","3:1","More than one of the above","None of the above","A","Independent assortment of unlinked alleles yields an F2 phenotypic ratio of 9:3:3:1.","BPSC TRE 1.0 Secondary Science, Q. 115","official_pyq_verified","Verified Official PYQ","Easy","2026-10-13T06:05:20Z"
"bpsc-sec-q-0004","bpsc-tre-secondary","bpsc-sec-phy","bpsc-sec-phy-c2","bpsc-sec-phy-t2","2024","TRE 3.0 (March 2024)","According to Faraday's laws of electromagnetic induction, the magnitude of induced electromotive force (EMF) in a closed circuit is directly proportional to:","The rate of change of magnetic flux through the circuit","The electric potential across the battery terminals","The total electrical resistance of the loop","More than one of the above","None of the above","A","Faraday's law states that induced EMF e = -dΦ/dt, proportional to the time rate of change of magnetic flux.","BPSC TRE 3.0 Secondary Science, Q. 79","official_pyq_verified","Verified Official PYQ","Easy","2026-10-13T06:05:20Z"
"bpsc-sec-q-0005","bpsc-tre-secondary","bpsc-sec-chem","bpsc-sec-chem-c2","bpsc-sec-chem-t2","2024","TRE 3.0 (March 2024)","What is the correct chemical formula of Plaster of Paris (POP), produced by heating Gypsum at 373 K?","CaSO₄·2H₂O","CaSO₄·½H₂O","CaSO₄·H₂O","More than one of the above","None of the above","B","Plaster of Paris is calcium sulphate hemihydrate, CaSO₄·½H₂O (or 2CaSO₄·H₂O). Gypsum is CaSO₄·2H₂O.","BPSC TRE 3.0 Secondary Science, Q. 93","official_pyq_verified","Verified Official PYQ","Easy","2026-10-13T06:05:20Z"
"bpsc-sec-q-0006","bpsc-tre-secondary","bpsc-sec-phy","bpsc-sec-phy-c2","bpsc-sec-phy-t3","2023","TRE 2.0 (Dec 2023)","Two resistors of resistance 6 Ω and 12 Ω are connected in parallel across a 12 V battery. What is the equivalent resistance of the combination and the total current supplied by the battery?","Equivalent Resistance = 4 Ω; Total Current = 3 A","Equivalent Resistance = 18 Ω; Total Current = 0.67 A","Equivalent Resistance = 4 Ω; Total Current = 48 A","More than one of the above","None of the above","A","1/R_eq = 1/6 + 1/12 = 3/12 = 1/4 => R_eq = 4 Ω. I = V / R_eq = 12 / 4 = 3 A.","BPSC TRE 2.0 Secondary Science (Class 9-10, Q. 71)","official_pyq_verified","Verified Official PYQ","Moderate","2026-10-13T06:05:20Z"
