"bpsc-sec-q-0322","bpsc-tre-secondary","bpsc-sec-phy","bpsc-sec-phy-c2","bpsc-sec-phy-t6","","","A convex lens has a focal length f = +12 cm. An object is placed at a distance of u = 23 cm in front of the lens. What is the power of the lens and the nature of the image formed? (Problem 1)","Power = +8.33 D; Real and inverted image","Power = -8.33 D; Virtual and erect image","Power = +16.67 D; Highly magnified image","More than one of the above","None of the above","A","Step 1: Power of a lens P = 1 / f(in metres) = 100 / f(in cm) = 100 / 12 = +8.33 D.
Step 2: Since the object is placed beyond the focal point (u = -23 cm vs f = +12 cm), a convex lens forms a real, inverted image on the other side of the lens.","","original_practice","Verified Syllabus Practice","Moderate","2026-10-13T06:05:20Z"
"bpsc-sec-q-0323","bpsc-tre-secondary","bpsc-sec-phy","bpsc-sec-phy-c2","bpsc-sec-phy-t6","","","A convex lens has a focal length f = +14 cm. An object is placed at a distance of u = 26 cm in front of the lens. What is the power of the lens and the nature of the image formed? (Problem 2)","Power = +7.14 D; Real and inverted image","Power = -7.14 D; Virtual and erect image","Power = +14.29 D; Highly magnified image","More than one of the above","None of the above","A","Step 1: Power of a lens P = 1 / f(in metres) = 100 / f(in cm) = 100 / 14 = +7.14 D.
Step 2: Since the object is placed beyond the focal point (u = -26 cm vs f = +14 cm), a convex lens forms a real, inverted image on the other side of the lens.","","original_practice","Verified Syllabus Practice","Moderate","2026-10-13T06:05:20Z"
