"bpsc-sec-q-0792","bpsc-tre-secondary","bpsc-sec-chem","bpsc-sec-chem-c2","bpsc-sec-chem-t7","","","What are the general molecular formulas for an alkane and an alkyne containing 3 carbon atoms respectively? (Problem 1)","Alkane: C_3H_8, Alkyne: C_3H_4","Alkane: C_3H_6, Alkyne: C_3H_8","Alkane: C_3H_4, Alkyne: C_3H_6","More than one of the above","None of the above","A","General formulas for aliphatic hydrocarbons:
• Alkanes (saturated): C_n H_{2n+2} → for n=3: C_3H_8.
• Alkenes (double bond): C_n H_{2n} → C_3H_6.
• Alkynes (triple bond): C_n H_{2n-2} → for n=3: C_3H_4.","","original_practice","Verified Syllabus Practice","Easy","2026-10-13T06:05:20Z"
